From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 13:59:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] krtld: do not allocate for an empty relocation section

`get_syms()` reads every `SHT_RELA`/`SHT_REL` section into a temporary
buffer sized by `sh_size`, without first checking that the section has
any content.  For a zero length section that is a `kobj_alloc(0)`, and
once krtld is out of its standalone phase `kobj_alloc()` is
`kmem_alloc()`, so a DEBUG kernel prints

    WARNING: kmem_alloc(): sleeping allocation with size of 0; see
    kmem_zerosized_log for details

once for every such section in every module loaded after boot.

Empty relocation sections are ordinary ELF: they appear whenever an
object's DWARF is *emptied* rather than removed -- the usual way to
strip an illumos module without disturbing the section table, since
removing sections breaks `sh_link`, the `DT_NEEDED` strings the link
editor parks past the end of `.strtab`, and the layout of `unix` --
which leaves each `.rela.debug_*` present with `sh_size` of zero.  A
kernel built that way carries four to six of them per module; a boot
that loads ~90 modules past `kmem_ready` therefore emits ~400 of these
warnings, each a synchronous `cmn_err()` to the console.  On an
emulated 16550 that measured at 3.1ms a line, or 1.27s of a 15s boot.

Skip the allocation and the read, which is what the section deserves
either way: `do_relocations()` computes `nreloc` as zero for it and,
for the `.rela.debug_*` case, skips it outright because the section it
relocates is not `SHF_ALLOC`.  Nothing observes `sh_addr` in between,
and `kmem_alloc(0)` returned `NULL` for it before this change anyway.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5 (claude-opus-5)
---
 usr/src/uts/common/krtld/kobj.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/usr/src/uts/common/krtld/kobj.c b/usr/src/uts/common/krtld/kobj.c
index 63170de612..a75b32a8a4 100644
--- a/usr/src/uts/common/krtld/kobj.c
+++ b/usr/src/uts/common/krtld/kobj.c
@@ -2571,6 +2571,19 @@ get_syms(struct module *mp, struct _buf *file)
 			if (shp->sh_addr)
 				continue;
 
+			/*
+			 * An empty relocation section has nothing to read
+			 * and nothing for do_relocations() to apply, and
+			 * kobj_alloc() of zero bytes is a deprecated
+			 * kmem_alloc(9F) that a DEBUG kernel warns about
+			 * once per call.  Such sections are common in
+			 * objects whose DWARF has been emptied rather than
+			 * removed, since that leaves the matching
+			 * ".rela.debug_*" section present but zero length.
+			 */
+			if (shp->sh_size == 0)
+				continue;
+
 			/* KM_TMP since kobj_free'd in do_relocations */
 			shp->sh_addr = (Addr)
 			    kobj_alloc(shp->sh_size, KM_WAIT|KM_TMP);
